  "query_preview": "guidance still shows a weakening northern stream shortwave \ntrough passing through our area Sunday into Monday. Rain chances are \nstill low (20-30%) at this time, but the wave and its cold front \ncould squeeze out some moisture with showers in the Sunday/Monday \ntime frame. A few areas along and north of Hwy 82 will have a better \nchance for some brief scattered convection (40-50%). Rainfall totals \nin general will be between 0.10-0.25 inches across our CWA which \nwill not be enough to help alleviate ongoing drought conditions. The \nlatest U.S. Drought Monitor continues to show severe to exceptional \ndrought conditions across our entire area including portions of \nsoutheast AR and all of our northeast LA parishes. Expect conditions \nto worsen through the mid-week given the lack of rainfall in the \nforecast.\n\nConfidence in the pattern heading into mid next week still remains \nlow, as a progressive northern stream and strong southern jet stream \nprevail over the CONUS. Temperature forecast is for \"near normal\" \nbarring any significant systems. Dry conditions will continue \nto persist across the region heading into Thursday. /CR/NF/",
